{"candidateAnswer":"Evan's son was injured.","evidence":"[D7:1 | 4:20 pm on 15 August, 2023] Evan: Hey Sam, what's up? It's been a few days since we talked. How have you been? Life's been tough lately - my son had a soccer accident last Saturday and hurt his ankle, it was tough seeing him hurt! I just been looking after him and taking him to the doctor. As a dad, it's hard to watch your kid go through something like that.\n[D7:9 | 4:20 pm on 15 August, 2023] Evan: Thanks, Sam. His ankle is getting better, but still sore. It was rough at first, but thank goodness it was nothing serious.\n[D7:10 | 4:20 pm on 15 August, 2023] Sam: Glad to hear his ankle is getting better. It's hard seeing someone we care about hurt. Look after yourself too, yeah? We gotta look after our health.\n[D9:2 | 10:18 am on 27 August, 2023] Evan: Wow, Sam, great! Glad your new diet/exercise is going well. As for me, I've hit a sore spot lately. Twisted my knee last Friday and it's really painful, so it's been tough to stay consistent with my usual fitness routine. It's really frustrating because staying active is like, mega-important to me.\n[D11:2 | 8:57 pm on 6 October, 2023] Evan: Hey Sam! That's awesome about your healthier eating! For me, I had a setback last week - messed up my knee playing b-ball with the kids. It's been tough to stay active since. I really miss going on adventures like we did last year - good times with the family!\n[D11:3 | 8:57 pm on 6 October, 2023] Sam: Hey Evan, sorry to hear about your knee. It must be tough. Are there any ways to stay active while you heal up?","itemId":"urn:uuid:1e7f2b05-f55d-5dd8-8294-d1378a37597d","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:ab29a67f669a19e1c644d0aad21d7dadbe06cb10950f284edc0b2b3fe2b6f38e","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Who was injured in Evan's family?","referenceAnswer":"Evan's son and Evan himself","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"ab29a67f669a19e1c644d0aad21d7dadbe06cb10950f284edc0b2b3fe2b6f38e"}}]}